DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20261209T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20261209T194500
SUMMARY:Nutcracker: Cast A Dress Rehearsal – ACT I Cast A (Mandatory 
 – Production Week)
LOCATION:Robinson Center
DESCRIPTION:*** THIS DAY ***\nCALL TIME 6:00 PM — be checked in and bac
 kstage by then. ARRIVE BY 5:45 PM.\nOn stage: 7:00 PM–7:45 PM.\nACT I 
 Dress Run\; In Performance Costumes\, Hair and Makeup.\nMANDATORY — pr
 oduction week.\n\n*** STANDING RULES ***\nBA: Call Time is the time danc
 ers should be check-in and backstage - Arrive 15 minutes before Call Tim
 e.\nBA: Mandatory Rehearsals (1st Rehearsal\, Rehearsals after Thanksgiv
 ing and Production Week Rehearsals and Performances).\nAll Casts are cal
 led unless a cast is named.\nSUBJECT TO CHANGE — the BA master schedul
 e\, the weekly BA emails and the BA portal are the official source. Mast
 er: https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1xWFCPfY5m0aK9d5dnxvALNre-6-N
 7Cl0kkw24rvm6cE/\n\n*** COSTUME / HAIR / MAKEUP — Mice ***\nMice — C
 ostume (you provide): Pink/Flesh Seamless Tights Black Camisole Leotard 
 Male Mice: white ballet shirt\, black shorts\, pink tights\; Shoes: Pink
  Ballet Shoes\; Makeup: Light Stage Makeup Men's Light Stage Makeup\; Ha
 ir: Male: Hair out of the eyes Female: High Bun\, No Part\; Accessories 
 (BA provides): Gray Gloves\nLight Stage Makeup Instruction Sheet:\n• P
 owder matching skintone\n• Light brown eye shadow applied to the creas
 e with an eye shadow brush\n• Dark Brown/Black eyeliner and black masc
 ara. No fake lashes.\n• Blush on the cheeks (be sure to apply plenty s
 o dancer doesn’t look washed out in the stage lights)\n• Red or Dark
  Red lipstick\nMen's Stage Makeup:\n• Dark Brown/Black eyeliner - appl
 y from corner to corner\n• Brown or tan under cheek bone to create sha
 dow and accentuate the jaw line\n• Brown eye liner around lips and nud
 e/flesh colored lipstick\n• *Men will not look like they are wearing m
 akeup. It will help the face be seen from the stage.\nDancers of Color m
 ay wear flesh tone tights and flesh tone ballet shoes.\nCostume Care Gui
 delines:\n• Handle costume pieces with care while changing to prevent 
 damage to delicate fabrics\n• Promptly notify Ballet Arkansas in the e
 vent of costume damage at the point of discovery\, no matter how signifi
 cant\n• Never throw costumes or accessories on the floor\, or hang cos
 tumes by their elastic straps\n• Refrain from sitting on the floor whi
 le in costume\n• Do not attempt to alter\, mend\, clean\, or launder a
 ny costume or accessory\n• Never apply stage make-up while in costume 
 and shall take great care to refrain from smudging make-up on costume du
 ring its removal\n• Refrain from the use of spray perfume or cologne w
 hile in costume\n• Never wear any garment not assigned to cast member\
 n• Do not handle or consume food or beverage while in costume\, with t
 he exception of water\n• Do not remove costumes from their assigned dr
 essing rooms or from the theater\n• Remove all bobby pins used to secu
 re head pieces and wigs following their use\n• Return all headpieces t
 o their assigned bags\n• Comply fully with any and all updates to Ball
 et Arkansas’ wardrobe policies\n• Do not pack markers\, paints\, col
 ored drinks or anything that may damage or stain costumes.
