 , ANGELS.\nMANDATORY — production week.\n\n*** STANDING RULES ***\nBA:
  Call Time is the time dancers should be check-in and backstage - Arrive
  15 minutes before Call Time.\nBA: Mandatory Rehearsals (1st Rehearsal\,
  Rehearsals after Thanksgiving and Production Week Rehearsals and Perfor
 mances).\nAll Casts are called unless a cast is named.\nSUBJECT TO CHANG
 E — the BA master schedule\, the weekly BA emails and the BA portal ar
 e the official source. Master: https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1x
 WFCPfY5m0aK9d5dnxvALNre-6-N7Cl0kkw24rvm6cE/\n\n*** COSTUME / HAIR / MAKE
 UP — Mice ***\nMice — Costume (you provide): Pink/Flesh Seamless Tig
 hts Black Camisole Leotard Male Mice: white ballet shirt\, black shorts\
 , pink tights\; Shoes: Pink Ballet Shoes\; Makeup: Light Stage Makeup Me
 n's Light Stage Makeup\; Hair: Male: Hair out of the eyes Female: High B
 un\, No Part\; Accessories (BA provides): Gray Gloves\nLight Stage Makeu
 p Instruction Sheet:\n• Powder matching skintone\n• Light brown eye 
 shadow applied to the crease with an eye shadow brush\n• Dark Brown/Bl
 ack eyeliner and black mascara. No fake lashes.\n• Blush on the cheeks
  (be sure to apply plenty so dancer doesn’t look washed out in the sta
 ge lights)\n• Red or Dark Red lipstick\nMen's Stage Makeup:\n• Dark 
 Brown/Black eyeliner - apply from corner to corner\n• Brown or tan und
 er cheek bone to create shadow and accentuate the jaw line\n• Brown ey
 e liner around lips and nude/flesh colored lipstick\n• *Men will not l
 ook like they are wearing makeup. It will help the face be seen from the
  stage.\nDancers of Color may wear flesh tone tights and flesh tone ball
 et shoes.\nCostume Care Guidelines:\n• Handle costume pieces with care
  while changing to prevent damage to delicate fabrics\n• Promptly noti
 fy Ballet Arkansas in the event of costume damage at the point of discov
 ery\, no matter how significant\n• Never throw costumes or accessories
  on the floor\, or hang costumes by their elastic straps\n• Refrain fr
 om sitting on the floor while in costume\n• Do not attempt to alter\, 
 mend\, clean\, or launder any costume or accessory\n• Never apply stag
 e make-up while in costume and shall take great care to refrain from smu
 dging make-up on costume during its removal\n• Refrain from the use of
  spray perfume or cologne while in costume\n• Never wear any garment n
 ot assigned to cast member\n• Do not handle or consume food or beverag
 e while in costume\, with the exception of water\n• Do not remove cost
 umes from their assigned dressing rooms or from the theater\n• Remove 
 all bobby pins used to secure head pieces and wigs following their use\n
 • Return all headpieces to their assigned bags\n• Comply fully with 
 any and all updates to Ballet Arkansas’ wardrobe policies\n• Do not 
 pack markers\, paints\, colored drinks or anything that may damage or st
 ain costumes.
